WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.133
You've got a model connected.

2
00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:05.000
Let's close the loop and actually talk to it — and cover the three errors you might hit on the way.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.774
Pick a model from the selector at the top of the chat, type a message, and press Enter.

4
00:00:09.774 --> 00:00:14.000
Nothing more to it — this is the plain chat you already know from other apps.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.630
The reply streams in live and renders as formatted markdown — headings, lists, and syntax-highlighted code blocks.

6
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.000
Ask it for a snippet to show that off on camera.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.874
Three errors catch almost everyone at least once.

8
00:00:23.874 --> 00:00:27.124
“No provider configured” means you skipped connecting a model — go back to Providers.

9
00:00:27.124 --> 00:00:30.565
“Connection refused” means your local server, Ollama or LM Studio, isn't actually running.

10
00:00:30.565 --> 00:00:33.165
And a 401 or 403 means a bad key, or a cloud account with no credit.

11
00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:35.000
Each one tells you exactly which of those it is.

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:35.882
That's a plain chat.

13
00:00:35.882 --> 00:00:41.000
Next episode is the big one — we give the model a tool, and watch it stop being a chat box and start being an agent.

